<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khuzestan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Khuzistan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khuzestan, historically Khuzistan, is a province of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> at the head of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a>, watered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karun-river">Karun River</a>. It was the heartland of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susa">Susa</a> as its chief city, and later a rich province of the Achaemenid, Sasanian and Islamic empires, famous for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> cane and textiles. Today it is the centre of Iran's oil industry and has a large Arab population.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khuzestan.jpg" alt="Khuzestan" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: درفش کاویانی · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shush_Castle_Darafsh_(25).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
